Runtime dependencies of this work
---------------------------------

**None.**
The Go module has no third-party imports (`go.sum` does not exist), and the
frontend makes no external requests: everything it needs is embedded in the
binary. See "Vendored frontend assets" below.


git
---

This program invokes the `git` binary as a *separate process* (`os/exec`). It
does not link or embed any Git code. Git is GPL-2.0; running a GPL program as a
subprocess does not make this work a derivative of it. Git is not distributed
with this work.


Vendored frontend assets
------------------------

These are copied into `web/vendor/` by `tools/vendor.sh` and embedded into the
binary. **Nothing is fetched from a network at runtime** — a tamper-evidence
product that pulls its stylesheet from a third-party CDN has a supply-chain hole,
and the whole argument of this project is "do not trust third parties".

| Component | Version | Licence | Licence text |
|---|---|---|---|
| Beer CSS | 5.0.3 | MIT | `web/vendor/beer/LICENSE` |
| material-dynamic-colors | 1.1.4 | MIT | `web/vendor/beer/LICENSE` |
| Bricolage Grotesque | v9 | SIL OFL 1.1 | `web/vendor/fonts/LICENSE` |
| Martian Mono | v6 | SIL OFL 1.1 | `web/vendor/fonts/LICENSE` |
| Roboto Flex | v30 | SIL OFL 1.1 | `web/vendor/fonts/LICENSE` |

Per-font copyright notices are in `web/vendor/fonts/NOTICE`.

To refresh them, run `tools/vendor.sh` and commit the result — the repository is
the source of truth, not the CDN. CI fails if any file under `web/` references an
external URL.

Note on the icon fonts: Beer CSS ships Material Symbols subsets. Their upstream
terms are Google's; they are redistributed here under the same MIT-licensed
package the Beer CSS distribution carries.
